  "id": "grade-inflation",
  "term": "grade inflation",
  "definition": "Grade inflation is a rise in awarded grades that does not reflect a matching rise in students’ ability or the quality of their work. It is usually seen as higher average GPAs or more top grades, which can crowd the upper end of the grading scale.",
